th kinds of report usually mean a dock fault rather than a bike fault.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-003\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Ask the rider to read the code on the dock display.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"This instruction is in the support desk document, so the support desk asks the rider, not the field crew as the claim states.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-004\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A dock showing E2 has a jammed locking pin.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states this verbatim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-005\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A dock showing E4 has lost power to\\nthe point.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states this verbatim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-006\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"E2 is a mechanical fault\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states that E2 is a mechanical fault.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-007\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"E4 is an electrical one\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states that E4 is an electrical fault.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-008\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"they are\\nescalated differently\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states that E2 and E4 are escalated differently.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-009\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Free the pin with the service key\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a's section on clearing E2 in the field says to free the pin with the service key.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-010\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"cycle the dock twice\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a's section on clearing E2 in the field says to cycle the dock twice.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-011\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"If the dock takes a\\nbike and releases it on both cycles, close the fault on your handheld.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states this with the same meaning.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-012\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Raise an E2 to the field crew.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The support desk document instructs raising an E2 to the field crew.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-013\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Escalate E2 to the workshop after 2 failed attempts.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states this verbatim, though source_b has the desk escalate to the workshop after 3 field crew attempts.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-014\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Do not keep cycling a dock\\nthat has failed twice\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a, the field crew document, instructs not to keep cycling a dock that has failed twice.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-015\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"repeated forcing bends the pin\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states that repeated forcing bends the pin.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-016\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"turns a 20 minute\\nworkshop job into a replacement\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states that repeated forcing turns a 20 minute workshop job into a replacement.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-017\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"E4 is never a field fix\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a's section heading states this verbatim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-018\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Report E4 to the electrical contractor the same day.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states this, and source_b agrees.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-019\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Field crew do not open the\\npower enclosure under any circumstances.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a states this verbatim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-020\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A rider charged for a journey that ended at a faulted dock gets the journey\\nrefunded.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_b states this verbatim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-021\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Refund at the time of the call\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_b instructs that the refund is given at the time of the call.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-022\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"do not wait for the fault to be\\nconfirmed\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_b says not to wait for the fault to be confirmed before refunding.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-023\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The support desk takes a station out of service in the app when more than half\\nits docks are faulted.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_b states this verbatim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-024\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Tell the support desk before you do this, not after.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"Source_a, addressed to field crew, says to tell the support desk before taking a station out of service, not after.\"}]}","ttft_ms":7160,"type":"result","duration_ms":21172,"uuid":"f6416441-3fe3-456c-9a22-56d2b3e7acc4","ttft_stream_ms":1634,"time_to_request_ms":95,"first_content_frame_ms":1634,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
